# Board #81: the gesture scripts 11-13 were commissioned as and could not express.
#
# CLICK A COMPONENT'S LABEL, RETYPE IT, COMMIT WITH RETURN — through the real Text Tool, on both
# sides, byte-matched against 4.1.0. Scripts 11, 12 and 13 each say in their own header that this
# was the script they wanted and that three blockers made it unwritable. All three are fixed:
# `EditBridge.java` obstacles 4 (`Canvas.getGraphics()` was null) and 5 (the fabricated `Frame`
# had a null `attrTable`), and the new `type` / `key return` operations. Those three rows keep
# their place — they gate `setattr` on `label`, `labelloc` and `facing`, which this does not touch
# — but they gate the *attribute*, and this gates the *placement*.
#
# ── WHY A CLICK GATES THE PLACEMENT AND A `setattr` DOES NOT ────────────────────────────────
#
# `13-label-tunnel` says of itself: "It does **not** exercise `Tunnel.labelPlacement`, and it would
# stay green if that placement were wrong." A click fixes exactly that.
# `InstanceTextField.getTextCaret` hit-tests the click against the label's own box
# (`InstanceTextField.java:113-118`), so the caret opens only if the box is where 4.1.0 puts it —
# and `TextTool.mousePressed`'s third arm (`TextTool.java:296-307`) turns a miss into a brand-new
# free-standing `Text` annotation rather than a silent no-op. A wrong placement therefore does not
# weaken this row, it changes the saved file structurally.
#
# MEASURED, not asserted. Each arm re-run with only the click moved, still inside the component
# body, everything else identical:
#
#   Tunnel, click (307,300) -> (320,300):
#       <comp name="Tunnel"><a name="label" val="T"/>            (unchanged — the retype vanished)
#       <comp lib="9" loc="(320,300)" name="Text"><a name="text" val="CLK"/>    (+ a whole comp)
#   Register, click (230,245) -> (230,275):
#       the same shape — label stays "A", a `Text` appears at the click.
#
# ── THE TWO COMPONENTS, AND WHY THESE TWO ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
#   * **Tunnel** — `TunnelAttributes.configureLabel()` (`TunnelAttributes.java:47-78`), which is
#     NOT the shared `Instance.computeLabelTextField` path: its `labelX`/`labelY` are offsets from
#     the anchor by `Tunnel.ARROW_MARGIN`, H_LEFT and V_CENTER_OVERALL. Measured box for `T` at
#     (300,300): starts at x=305, vertically centred on y=300. This is the placement
#     `13-label-tunnel` named as ungated, and it is now gated byte-exactly.
#   * **Register with `labelloc center`** — `Instance.computeLabelTextField`'s `LABEL_CENTER` arm
#     (`Instance.java:138-142`), i.e. the shared path all ~87 of the memory/io/TTL/Tunnel
#     placements added by board #78 run through, reached from a memory factory.
#
# **`labelloc center` is not decoration and not a convenience — read `14-caret-retype-detached-
# label.script` before changing it.** The DEFAULT `labelloc` for a Register is `north`, which puts
# the label box entirely OUTSIDE the component body, and that case is a measured port defect. It
# has its own script, and that script is red on purpose. This one uses `center` so that the rest
# of the pipeline — hit test, clear, type, commit — is gated green and independently, instead of
# being hidden behind the one defect.
#
# The clicks sit on the ALIGNMENT ANCHOR rather than at the box centre, deliberately: y=300 is the
# Tunnel field's vertical centre and (230,245) is the Register field's H_CENTER/V_CENTER anchor, so
# the hit stays inside the box under any text-measurement engine whose glyph advances are within a
# few units of AWT's. This gate is meant to catch a wrong *placement*, not to assert that CoreText
# and AWT measure "Q7" to the same pixel.
#
# ── WHY THE FIELD IS CLEARED WITH BACKSPACE AND DELETE ──────────────────────────────────────
#
# Where the caret lands on a click is `GraphicsUtil.getTextPosition(g, ...)` — a character index
# derived from font metrics, which AWT and CoreText need not agree on. `key backspace` x2 then
# `key delete` x2 empties the field and leaves the caret at 0 from ANY starting index (both are
# no-ops on an empty field), so everything after the click is metric-independent. Two of each for
# a one-character label is deliberate slack: the count only has to be at least the label's length.
# See `EditBridge.java`'s script-language section for the full argument.
tool	add:Tunnel
toolattr	label	T
click	300	300
tool	add:Register
toolattr	label	A
toolattr	labelloc	center
click	200	200
tool	text
click	307	300
key	backspace
key	backspace
key	delete
key	delete
type	CLK
key	return
click	230	245
key	backspace
key	backspace
key	delete
key	delete
type	Q7
key	return
